Here is what `SmartCalendar.vue` actually does for **leave / cancelled** and **ClassSession**.

---

## 1. Filtering `cancelled` (and not `leave`) on ClassSession rows

`sessionDatesSetByCourseId` builds each course’s “real session dates” from `sessionDatesByCourseId` (filled by the ClassSession API). Only rows whose `status` is **`cancelled`** are dropped; **`leave` is not filtered here**.

```1058:1072:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
/** 每門課的「實際上課日」集合（僅此 N 堂會顯示）：使用共用工具確保與課程管理一致 */
const sessionDatesSetByCourseId = computed(() => {
  const out = {};
  courses.value.forEach((c) => {
    const cid = c.id != null ? String(c.id) : '';
    const rows = sessionDatesByCourseId.value[cid];
    if (!Array.isArray(rows) || rows.length === 0) return;
    const dates = rows
      .filter((row) => String(row?.status || '').toLowerCase() !== 'cancelled')
      .map((row) => String(row?.session_date || '').slice(0, 10))
      .filter(Boolean);
    const dateSet = new Set(dates);
    if (dateSet && dateSet.size) out[cid] = dateSet;
  });
  return out;
});
```

---

## 2. Hiding base blocks when a **schedules** exception is `leave` or `rescheduled`

In **week** view, `filteredCourses` merges recurring courses with `exceptions` (`schedules`: leaves, reschedules, etc.). If an exception exists for that course + date with `status === 'leave'` **or** `status === 'rescheduled'`, the normal base occurrence is **not** added (`!hasLeaveOrReschedule && !hasScheduledExc`).

```1356:1382:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
        const targetYmd = String(targetDate).slice(0, 10);
        const hasLeaveOrReschedule = exceptions.value.some(ex =>
          (ex.status === 'leave' || ex.status === 'rescheduled') &&
          (ex.student_course_id == null ? false : String(ex.student_course_id) === cid) &&
          toYmd(ex.schedule_date) === targetDate
        );
        const hasScheduledExc = exceptions.value.some(ex =>
          ex.status === 'scheduled' &&
          (ex.student_course_id != null && String(ex.student_course_id) === cid) &&
          toYmd(ex.schedule_date) === targetDate
        );
        if (sessionSet) {
          if (!sessionSet.has(targetYmd)) continue;
          const lastDate = courseLastSessionDate.value[cid] ?? (sessionSet.size ? Array.from(sessionSet).sort().pop() : null);
          if (lastDate != null && targetYmd > lastDate) continue;
          if (!hasLeaveOrReschedule && !hasScheduledExc) mergedList.push({ ...c, day_of_week: dow, days_of_week: [dow], is_base: true });
          continue;
        }
        const isFirstDay = c.first_class_date && String(targetDate).trim() === String(c.first_class_date).trim();
        const isRecurringDay = days.includes(dow);
        if (!isFirstDay && !isRecurringDay) continue;
        const isBeforeStart = c.first_class_date && String(targetDate).trim() < String(c.first_class_date).trim();
        const overSessionLimit = isOverSessionLimit(c.id, targetDate);
        if (!hasLeaveOrReschedule && !hasScheduledExc && !isBeforeStart && !overSessionLimit) {
          mergedList.push({ ...c, day_of_week: dow, days_of_week: [dow], is_base: true });
        }
```

**Scheduled (rescheduled-to) rows** on a date where the same course already has **`leave`** are also suppressed:

```1385:1408:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
    // 2. Add extra and scheduled (rescheduled-to) classes that fall onto this week's dates
    //    已刪除的課程（student_course_id 不在 courses 內）不顯示調課
    //    若該日該課程已請假，則不顯示該筆調課/加課
    const courseIds = new Set(courses.value.map(c => c.id));
    const hasLeave = (date, courseId) => exceptions.value.some(ex =>
      ex.status === 'leave' && toYmd(ex.schedule_date) === date && ex.student_course_id == courseId
    );
    ...
    for (let dow = 1; dow <= 7; dow++) {
      const targetDate = getDisplayDateFull(dow);
      const dayExceptions = exceptions.value.filter(ex =>
        toYmd(ex.schedule_date) === targetDate &&
        ex.status === 'scheduled' &&
        (ex.student_course_id == null || courseIds.has(Number(ex.student_course_id))) &&
        !hasLeave(targetDate, ex.student_course_id) &&
        (!isTeacher.value || !currentTeacherId.value || String(ex.teacher_id) === currentTeacherId.value)
      );
```

There is **no** comparable filter on `exceptions` for `status === 'cancelled'` in these snippets; cancellation is handled on **ClassSession** rows for date sets (above), and week merge logic keys off **`leave` / `rescheduled` / `scheduled`** on `schedules`.

---

## 3. “Display” of leave in the calendar grid

The **week grid** only renders student / subject / class type on each block. There is **no** template branch that labels a block as “請假” or styles leave differently; leave is reflected by **omitting** that occurrence from `filteredCourses` (see above).

Day / week overview cell content:

```147:161:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
                <div
                  v-for="(course, cIdx) in getCoursesForTeacherAt(teacher.id, h)"
                  :key="course.id"
                  class="course-block"
                  :style="getTeacherCourseBlockStyle(course, teacher.id, h, cIdx)"
                  ...
                >
                  <div class="cb-student">{{ course.student_name }}</div>
                  <div class="cb-detail">{{ getSubjectLabel(course.subject) }}</div>
                  <div class="cb-type">{{ classTypeLabel(course.class_type) }}</div>
                </div>
```

`getCoursesForTeacherAt` (and counts) are driven by **`filteredCourses`**, which is where leave removes items:

```1165:1198:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
const getCoursesForTeacherAt = (teacherId, hour) => {
  return filteredCourses.value.filter(c => {
    if (c.teacher_id !== teacherId) return false;
    if (parseHour(c.start_time) !== hour) return false;
    if (c.day_of_week !== selectedDow.value) return false;
    return true;
  });
};
...
const getDayCourseCount = (dow) => {
  return filteredCourses.value.filter(c => c.day_of_week === dow).length;
};
```

Separate UI: **請假** button and leave **modal** (workflow, not a “leave” chip on the grid):

```463:525:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
            <button class="action-btn leave" @click="openLeaveModal">📋 請假</button>
...
    <!-- ===== Leave Modal (請假) ===== -->
    <div v-if="showLeaveModal" class="modal-overlay" @click.self="showLeaveModal = false">
...
          <button class="primary" @click="submitLeave">確認請假</button>
```

Submit sets `schedules` row `status: 'leave'`:

```2138:2148:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
    subject: leaveForm.value.subject,
    day_of_week: Number(leaveForm.value.day_of_week) || 1,
    start_time: leaveForm.value.start_time,
    end_time: leaveForm.value.end_time,
    duration_hours: leaveForm.value.duration_hours || 2,
    class_type: leaveForm.value.class_type || 'one_on_one',
    status: 'leave',
...
    schedule_date: leaveForm.value.schedule_date,
```

---

## 4. ClassSession → calendar: load and use

**Load** (after courses + exceptions):

```1600:1620:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
  courses.value = courseList;
  exceptions.value = excData;

  // Single source of truth: class session dates come from backend ClassSession API.
  sessionDatesByCourseId.value = {};
  if (token && branchId && courseList.length > 0) {
    const ids = courseList.map((c) => Number(c?.id || 0)).filter((id) => id > 0);
    if (ids.length > 0) {
      try {
        const { byClass } = await fetchClassSessions({
          token,
          branchId,
          studentClassIds: ids,
          perPage: 2000,
        });
        sessionDatesByCourseId.value = byClass || {};
      } catch (_) {
        sessionDatesByCourseId.value = {};
      }
    }
  }
```

Import:

```659:659:/home/admin/frontend/src/pages/SmartCalendar.vue
import { fetchClassSessions } from '../lib/classSessionsApi';
```

Those ClassSession rows feed **`sessionDatesSetByCourseId`** (cancelled filtered out), which drives **which dates** count for **session / 堂數** courses inside **`filteredCourses`** (`sessionSet.has(targetYmd)`, `getSessionDateSetForCourse`, `courseLastSessionDate`, etc. as in the first snippet block of section 2).

---

**Summary:** **`cancelled`** ClassSession rows are excluded when building per-course session date sets. **`leave`** is handled mainly via **`schedules` / `exceptions`**, which **suppress** the base cell and certain rescheduled rows for that date; the grid does **not** render an explicit “leave” badge—leave shows as **no block** plus the **請假** modal flow. Calendar cells ultimately come from **`filteredCourses`** built from courses + exceptions + ClassSession-backed date sets.

